Today i practice 20 commands of linux
1) print : print the present working directory
2) ls : list file & command in the current directory
      ls -l : displat detail info about file & directory
3)cd : change the current directory to specfied diectory
  cd .. : go up one level in directory hieraechy
  cd ~ : go to the home directory
4)mkdire : make new directory
5)rm : remove a file
  rm -r : remove a directory & it's contents recursively
6)cp : copy a file or directory
  cp -r : copy a directory & it's content recrsively
7)mv : move or rename a file or directory
8)touch : create a file

B)FILE MANIPULATION :
1)cat : Display the contentof file
2)less file : view the content of file with pagination
3)head file : Display the first few lines of a file
4)tail file : display the last few lines of a file
5)grep pattern :search for a pattern in file
  grep -r pattern: search a pattern a file within a directory
 
c)TEXT EDITING:
1)nano file: open a file for editing with nano editor
2)vim file: open a file for editing with vim editor
  
D)SYSTEM INFORMATION:
1)uname : print system information
2)whoami:display the current user
3)df:display disk space
4)free:display memory space
5)uptime:show the system uptime

